  "final": "I added `clamp(value, lower, upper)` to `src/numbers.py`, kept `add` unchanged, and extended `checks/public.py`. `python3 checks/public.py` passes (prints `ok`, exit 0).\n\n**Change in `src/numbers.py`:**\n- `clamp` returns `lower` when `value < lower`, `upper` when `value > upper`, and `value` otherwise, so both bounds are inclusive.\n- If `lower > upper`, it raises `ValueError` before checking the value.\n- `add` is unchanged.\n\n**Checks added to `checks/public.py`:**\n- The original `add(2, 3) == 5` check is kept.\n- Values inside the range, on each bound, and below and above the range.\n- A degenerate range where `lower == upper`.\n- `clamp(1, 10, 0)` must raise `ValueError`.\n\nOnly `src/` and `checks/` were modified.",
